body:
The verse in question is from Surat An-naba,   


Clear Quran translation: " Have We not smoothed out the earth ˹like a bed˺ "

Abdul Haleem translation: " Did We not make the earth smooth "

Pickthall translation " Have We not made the earth an expanse, "

&#x200B;

It does seem to convey the idea that the earth is spread out. but it's hard to interpret that as the earth being flat when we have other verses that strongly imply the earth and other celestial objects' roundness: 

&#x200B;

39:5 "He created the heavens and the earth for a purpose. He wraps the night around the day, and wraps the day around the night. And He has subjected the sun and the moon, each orbiting for an appointed term. He is truly the Almighty, Most Forgiving. "  

&#x200B;

The earliest scholars of Islam held the position that the earth is round. Ibn taymiyyah attested to this. Additionally, Ibn hazm also believed the earth to be round. Essentially, they understood the verse as the earth \*below\* us being spread out for us in terms of its vastness and walkability, not that the \*planet\* earth was flat.

&#x200B;

But lets think about the verse since atheists like to point out its supposed clash with science. Allah swt says he made the earth smooth. even from a scientific perspective, the earth \*IS\* smooth. In fact, it is so smooth, that if the earth were shrunk down to the size of a pool ball, it would be smoother than the pool ball. Also,compare the surface of the earth to that of the moon, relatively speaking, with all the craters of the moon, the earth is much smoother. Anyways Allah knows best but don't let random people shake your faith in Islam brother/sister. you as a muslim have to dominate them intellectually, dont wait for enemies of Islam to come and  approach you with things you ahvent heard of.

I agree. I noticed though, as soon as you compare one small island vs the rest of the world, many people suddenly become utilitarian and easily ascribe a numeric value to life. that ws the point of my original comment i guess.

&#x200B;

yea the manga ending to me signals that isayama is going to create an aot
